" vimrc's Q now calls a real function (QuitBufferOrWindow) to fall back
" through the buffer list, which IdeaVim can't parse - overriding it here
" instead, since IdeaVim has no vim buffer-list model to fall back through
" anyway.
" This used to be an <expr> mapping calling expand('%') to tell an editable
" buffer (write & quit) from an unnamed one (quit without writing, since :wq
" there just fails with E32) - but IdeaVim doesn't implement expand(), or
" the ~600 other vimscript built-in functions, at all: confirmed against the
" IdeaVim maintainers' own vimscript-support notes. That made every Q throw
" E117: Unknown function: expand instead of running. (An earlier version
" also checked &readonly/!&modifiable first, matching real vim's
" QuitBufferOrWindow, but IdeaVim doesn't implement those options either and
" referencing &readonly threw E518: Unknown option.)
" Use IntelliJ actions instead of vimscript functions, since :action calls
" are the one thing proven reliable elsewhere in this file (m-, [c/]c, etc):
" save the current file (no-op if unmodified) and close its editor tab.
" IntelliJ editor tabs are basically never truly unnamed the way vim buffers
" can be, so this covers the cases the old <expr> version tried to split.
nnoremap Q :action SaveDocument<CR>:action CloseContent<CR>

